{
  "$schema": "https://aka.ms/codetour-schema",
  "title": "10 · Home server access decision",
  "description": "Request URL is / after onboarding or direct navigation.",
  "steps": [
    {
      "file": "apps/web/src/app/page.tsx",
      "line": 7,
      "title": "Home",
      "description": "Call serverSessionGateway() to construct the port, then await readAccess(gateway).\n\nTransition: server route calls policy"
    },
    {
      "file": "apps/web/src/features/auth/application/policy.ts",
      "line": 46,
      "title": "readAccess",
      "description": "Await gateway.read(); catch failure as unavailable. Returned identity determines access.\n\nTransition: calls gateway.read"
    },
    {
      "file": "apps/web/src/features/auth/infrastructure/session-gateway.ts",
      "line": 11,
      "title": "createSessionGateway.read",
      "description": "Await port.readAuth(); no valid userId → return anonymous without user lookup. Otherwise await port.readUser().\n\nTransition: calls server port"
    },
    {
      "file": "apps/web/src/features/auth/infrastructure/server-session.ts",
      "line": 8,
      "title": "serverSessionGateway.readAuth",
      "description": "This injected callback checks config then calls auth(treatPendingAsSignedOut:false). It returns to gateway.read. With valid userId, gateway.read then invokes the sibling readUser callback, which calls auth again then clerkClient().users.getUser. The factory itself is not called again here.\n\nTransition: server-only SDK boundary"
    },
    {
      "file": "apps/web/src/features/auth/infrastructure/session-gateway.ts",
      "line": 11,
      "title": "createSessionGateway.read",
      "description": "Validate matching user, primary email verification; pending session suppresses organizationId. Return normalized identity to readAccess.\n\nTransition: returns identity"
    },
    {
      "file": "apps/web/src/features/auth/application/policy.ts",
      "line": 46,
      "title": "readAccess",
      "description": "No user → anonymous; unverified → unverified; verified org → authenticated; verified no org → organization-required.\n\nTransition: returns AccessResult"
    },
    {
      "file": "apps/web/src/app/page.tsx",
      "line": 7,
      "title": "Home",
      "description": "Handle AccessResult: unavailable renders AuthUnavailable; anonymous redirects signin; org-required redirects picker; otherwise ClerkHome(verified=authenticated).\n\nTransition: redirect OR render"
    },
    {
      "file": "apps/web/src/features/auth/presentation/clerk-auth.tsx",
      "line": 66,
      "title": "ClerkHome",
      "description": "React renders HomeView using default useAuth readiness and sign-out callbacks. HomeView shows restoring/signedout/verified Home or verification-required state.\n\nTransition: React rendering"
    },
    {
      "title": "Branches and stop conditions",
      "description": "RootLayout/ClerkProvider are rendering context; the server access policy runs independently of the client visual gate.\n\nUnverified status renders ClerkHome with verified=false; this shows verification-required, not protected Home content.\n\nMalformed user/mismatch returns anonymous; SDK outage maps unavailable. No active organization → /organizations."
    }
  ]
}
